   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 7.5. Increased capacity of Member States to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks, institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">An inter-stakeholder coordination mechanism on fair and effective labour migration frameworks was established under the leadership of the Ministry of Overseas Pakistani and Human Resource Development (MOP&amp;HRD), including the National Vocational &amp;Technical Training Commission (NAVTTC), Employers&apos; Federation of Pakistan (EFP), Overseas Employment Corporation (OEC) and Bureau of Emigration and Overseas Employment (BE&amp;OE) in May 2023. A Steering Committee was established for the National Skills Passport Pilot, an initiative led by MOP&amp;HRD and the EFP. Steering Committee members include the MOP&amp;HRD, BE&amp;OE, Sindh Technical Education and Vocational Training Authority, NAVTTC, Employers&apos; Federation of Pakistan, and ILO. 
The NSP helps workers find better job opportunities through recognition of prior learning and validation of skills, by reskilling or upskilling. It reduces the role of intermediaries in local and international labour markets by creating a pool of professionals and a database of employers, connecting TEVET sectors and employers to collaborate closely and build synergies. 
EFP organized identified trades in consultation with stakeholders, ran an advocacy campaign for NSP among TEVET institutes in Sindh using digital tools.
EFP has organized awareness sessions and trained Assessors on existing competencies of identified trades to maintain quality assurance. 
EFP and Pakistan Workers Federations (PWF) signed an MOU on 24 August 2023 under the Workers Employers Bilateral Council of Pakistan, supporting joint efforts to promote safe and responsible migration, ensure social protection for migrant domestic workers and support businesses in countries of origin and destination. The MoU recognises migrant domestic workers as workers and seeks to protect their rights
In 2023 SDPI established a knowledge hub on labour migration in Pakistan to support evidence-based policymaking on labour migration aligned with international labour standards. The ILO, with support of the Swiss Development Cooperation (SDC), has provided technical support to the Government to raise awareness on safe, fair and regular pathways for labour migration and improving labour migration governance in Pakistan and to support the government&apos;s new interventions to improve labour migration and ensure safe and fair labour migration &#x2013; with a focused approach to expand overseas labour markets.  
ILO provided technical assistance to the Ministry of Federal Education and Professional Training, MOP&amp;HRD, BE&amp;OE, and NAVTTC. HEC, NAVTTC, STEVTA and the Pakistan Bureau of Statistics (PBS) to build their capacities to establish frameworks on labour mobility, skills standardization, and recognition of prior learning in Pakistan in support of the NSP pilot. Support was provided to prepare the South Asia reference qualification framework for recognition of prior learning, standardization skills, and training. 
ILO undertook advocacy and provided technical support to EFP and PWF to support the signature of the MoU.
ILO provided technical inputs to Sustainable Development Policy Institutes to establish knowledge hub. 
ILO also provided technical to development partners including IOM, ICMPD, and GIZ, actively supporting Government initiatives in improving services for migrant workers.  ILO has a leadership role in promoting fair and safe labour migration in line with ILO standards and multilateral guidelines</narrative>
